Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."cpc": contains one or more CPC symbols; filter for codes that begin with ‟A01B3”.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."assignee_harmonized": JSON/VARIANT array holding assignee dictionaries; flatten to reach the `"name"` key that will be grouped.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."filing_date": numeric YYYYMMDD; divide by 10000 (integer) to obtain the filing year.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."country_code": two‑letter publication country; count which country occurs most often in a given year for an assignee.  
• PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS."application_number": each row is one application; COUNT(*) gives number of applications.  
Typical conditions that will be used  
WHERE c.value::STRING ILIKE 'A01B3%'          -- keep only CPC codes that start with A01B3  
WHERE a.value:"name"::STRING ILIKE '%company%' -- fuzzy search on assignee name  
WHERE (p."filing_date" BETWEEN 19000101 AND 20991231) -- keep well‑formed dates  
AND p."country_code" IS NOT NULL  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows) that gradually build the logic needed for the final analysis.  

